diff --git a/.agents/skills/verify-release-gate/SKILL.md b/.agents/skills/verify-release-gate/SKILL.md
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..d189b0d8
--- /dev/null
+++ b/.agents/skills/verify-release-gate/SKILL.md
@@ -0,0 +1,81 @@
+---
+name: verify-release-gate
+description: Verify SRW release-gate worker and receipt lifecycle after changing the gate, scheduler, receipt identity, lock or deployment callers.
+---
+
+# Verify release gate receipt lifecycle
+
+Use the actual-code verifier rather than a second handwritten state model.
+Its CLI fixture creates a private Git repository under `TMPDIR` and calls the
+production receipt helper in separate Node processes. It checks a finite set
+of lifecycle transitions, not every possible process interleaving.
+
+## Covered code and sync
+
+Owners: `test_srw16_release_gate.js` (`runStep`, full-gate entry point),
+`scripts/srw_release_gate_runner.cjs` (`run`),
+`scripts/srw_release_gate_receipt.cjs` (`runWithReceipt`).
+The canonical lock owner remains `process_lock.js`.
+Initial source baseline before SRW-81: `bb5dad2cf5013d2d2c04c5c2ff9a7707bd9db595`.
+The task report records the exact implementation revision actually verified;
+move the sync record only after repeating the checks against changed code.
+
+Properties and harms:
+
+- Reuse requires an identical clean commit, Node version, lockfile, dependency
+  bytes and environment. A stale receipt could otherwise hide a regression.
+- Failed or interrupted work cannot publish a pass. A checkout change during
+  execution cannot inherit a clean pass.
+- Two callers for one clean identity execute one callback. Concurrent replay
+  could otherwise duplicate the expensive work.
+- The full gate retains all assertions and replays the complete corpus.
+  A receipt for a partial step is never a full-gate pass.
+
+## Run
+
+Run one heavy command at a time, from the repository root:
+
+```sh
+heavy --review node scripts/verify_srw_release_gate_receipt.cjs
+heavy --review node test_srw16_release_gate.js
+heavy --review node test_srw16_release_gate.js
+```
+
+The verifier must exit zero and print every scenario as passed, including cold
+execution, reuse, force, dirtiness, changed commit, Node/environment/dependency
+changes, lockfile change, callback failure, nonzero exit, mid-run drift,
+concurrent callers, publication failure and malformed receipts. It preserves failed fixture
+repositories under `TMPDIR` for inspection.
+
+The first full-gate call must execute if the identity has no receipt; the second
+must print `gate-receipt` with `cacheHit: true`. Read the receipt in
+`git rev-parse --git-common-dir` under `srw-release-gate-receipts` and confirm its
+HEAD SHA and Node version. A dirty checkout intentionally cannot demonstrate
+receipt reuse.
+
+For an intentional fresh measurement, add `--force --profile "$TMPDIR/gate.json"`.
+Do not raise worker concurrency beyond two or modify heavy safety thresholds.
+
+## Negative control and drift
+
+The verifier deliberately throws and sets a nonzero exit code, and asserts
+that neither action writes a receipt. It also mutates the tracked fixture during
+execution and requires failure. To verify the full gate after changing its
+assertion routing, archive the current committed source into a task-private Git
+checkout, restore locked dependencies there, change a known submitted-order
+expectation to an impossible value, commit that break, and run the full gate
+through heavy. Require a nonzero exit and no passing receipt for the broken SHA.
+Never introduce the break into canonical main or persistent paper state.
+
+If a verifier fails, inspect its preserved scratch repository and stdout.
+Distinguish a broken implementation from a fixture that no longer matches the
+helper contract. Never loosen an assertion or accept an incomplete corpus to
+make it pass. Apply maintain-formal-verification-skill when the owners drift.
+
+## Limits
+
+The fixture covers bounded actual subprocess transitions. It is not a proof
+against arbitrary filesystem mutation, a hostile writer to the Git directory,
+all signal timings, or every OS process schedule. The full gate proves local
+simulated execution only. Heavy admission, board invocation, deployment and
+live brokerage remain separate evidence layers.
