index 00000000..38ec3596
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/release_gate.md
@@ -0,0 +1,30 @@
+# Run the SRW release gate once per commit
+
+Run the same entry point for implementation, board checks, review and deployment:
+
+```sh
+~/.local/bin/heavy --review node test_srw16_release_gate.js
+```
+
+The entry point checks for a passing receipt before starting replay. A receipt proves the local deterministic gate at one exact Git commit. It does not prove CI, deployment, live delivery or broker execution. A rebase or merge creates a new commit and requires a new run.
+
+## What runs
+
+The runner preserves the complete real-post corpus and every existing expectation, rejection, deadline, restart, copy-trading, index-lotto and feature check. Independent checks run in separate Node processes, with at most two active workers inside one heavy admission. Stateful posts within a replay stay ordered. Each runtime keeps its own record and ledger files under `TMPDIR`.
+
+The default runs independent steps in filename order, the fastest measured candidate with two workers. `--schedule longest` starts the large replay groups first, and `--schedule grouped` runs the eight chase checks together to share their module setup. `--jobs 1` limits the runner to one worker. `--force` bypasses receipt reuse for an intentional measurement. `--profile "$TMPDIR/gate.json"` saves stage durations. Queueing and pauses belong to heavy and may add wall time beyond the admitted runtime.
+
+```sh
+~/.local/bin/heavy node test_srw16_release_gate.js --force --jobs 1 --profile "$TMPDIR/gate-serial.json"
+~/.local/bin/heavy node test_srw16_release_gate.js --force --profile "$TMPDIR/gate-parallel.json"
+```
+
+## Receipt lifecycle
+
+Receipts live outside the worktree in the Git common directory under `srw-release-gate-receipts`. Worktrees for the same repository share that directory. A passing result must match the commit, Node version and flags, lockfile, installed dependencies and relevant environment. Board, reviewer and terminal session identifiers do not change the replay inputs and are excluded from the environment fingerprint. A dirty checkout runs the checks and cannot publish or reuse a clean receipt. The runner checks identity again before publishing a result.
+
+An exclusive lock prevents concurrent callers from running the same clean identity twice. A waiting caller rechecks the receipt after the owner completes. Failed runs publish no receipt. Reuse checks structured metadata and reports the matching identity in the terminal.
+
+Use the existing gate command in deploy scripts. Copying a local receipt to another host does not establish a matching runtime. Changed Node or dependencies requires a fresh run there. Receipt files are local build evidence, not a security signature against someone with write access to the Git directory.
+
+See [the lifecycle chart](state-charts/release-gate.md) and [the verification procedure](../.agents/skills/verify-release-gate/SKILL.md).
