@@ -0,0 +1,33 @@
+# Release gate and receipt
+
+Owners: [`test_srw16_release_gate.js`](../../test_srw16_release_gate.js),
+[`srw_release_gate_runner.cjs`](../../scripts/srw_release_gate_runner.cjs),
+[`srw_release_gate_receipt.cjs`](../../scripts/srw_release_gate_receipt.cjs).
+
+```mermaid
+stateDiagram-v2
+  [*] --> Identify
+  Identify --> RunUncached: dirty checkout
+  Identify --> Lookup: clean identity
+  Lookup --> Passed: matching passing receipt
+  Lookup --> Wait: another owner holds lock
+  Wait --> Lookup: receipt or released owner
+  Lookup --> Run: acquired lock, no receipt
+  Run --> Failed: any worker fails or interruption
+  RunUncached --> Failed: any worker fails
+  RunUncached --> Passed: all assertions pass, no receipt
+  Run --> Recheck: every worker passed
+  Recheck --> Failed: checkout or runtime changed
+  Recheck --> Publish: identical clean identity
+  Publish --> Passed: atomic passing receipt
+  Passed --> [*]
+  Failed --> [*]
+```
+
+The runner starts at most two workers and waits for child closure before returning.
+It launches no further steps after a failure. Each replay retains source order,
+its full input corpus and all assertions. The receipt check applies only to the
+full entry point; individual `--step` invocations never publish a full-gate receipt.
+
+The [verification skill](../../.agents/skills/verify-release-gate/SKILL.md) records
+actual-code checks and their bounds. A chart alone is not execution evidence.
